# Green P1 result: the heavy-run guard refuses heavy commands outside heavy-run

Phase base SHA 05a3f38. Role base SHA 03e0353 (the Red commit). HEAD before the work was 03e0353 on branch feat/heavy-run-guard, and the tree was clean. The Red change 03e0353 lies inside phase_base_sha..HEAD. No push was made.

Green adds `heavyRunDecision(agent, command)` to `mods/measure-guard/hooks/guards.ts` (FR-1 to FR-7), copies it to both parity cores, and wires it into `Guard.onToolBefore` (FR-8). The matcher reads the words of a command segment. It strips the leading `NAME=value` assignments and one runner prefix (`npx`, `bunx`, or `bun x`). Then it applies the FR-3 classes in their fixed order. v1 guards direct commands only: no wrapper words, no shell `-c` recursion, and no non-path heavy-run `-c` recursion. The path form of heavy-run passes as a whole.

The plugin test `tests/tdd.test.ts` now runs its suite command through the heavy-run form. Two TDD tests used a bare `bun test` and `npm test`, and the heavy-run guard refuses those. The two Red test files were not changed.

